>
> The ABI is intentionally specification-first. The generated descriptor is

Commit message: "reserve family ID 2" is accurate, but nothing in this patch builds the new
generated .c/.h: `drivers/attestation/Makefile` is untouched, so these two files are never
compiled or even syntax-checked until patch 20. The .c references six undefined symbols
(`ctlv_attestation_tdx_op_pre`/post, `_priv_size`, `_pre_init`, `_init`, `_fini`, `_device_info`). Not a
build break, but 'specification-first' means ~130 lines of unverified generated C land one
patch before the thing that proves them. Consider folding into 0020, or at least compile-test
them here (e.g. build the .o with a stub). Also the message never says that the same patch
extends the UAPI `enum CTLV_FAMILY_ATTESTATION_TDX`, i.e. a permanent ABI commitment.

> linked with the provider implementation in the following patch.
