The `CTLV_IN_REF`/`CTLV_IN_HAS`/`CTLV_IN_BINARY` accessors (nine lines here) are generated for
attributes that exist only in a kernel-built reply nest (device-info fill). Nothing in
patch 20 (or anywhere) reads a device-info nest from a received message, so these are dead
generated code. Not a bug in this patch per se, but the generator should not emit
request-side readers for reply-only attr-sets (the same applies to the parent's header);
otherwise every family pays for unused inline helpers and a `stub_fill_schemas[0]`.members
dependency.

